 "prose": [
  {
   "tag": "a",
   "id": null,
   "text": "← Unfold"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h1",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Homotopy explorer"
  },
  {
   "tag": "label",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Category"
  },
  {
   "tag": "select",
   "id": "choose-category",
   "text": "HomotopiesCan / cannotHomotopy classes (maps)Homotopy types (spaces)"
  },
  {
   "tag": "label",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Example"
  },
  {
   "tag": "select",
   "id": "choose-example",
   "text": "Annulus ↔ circle — same typeDisk ↔ segment — same typeDisk ↔ point — same typeCircle with a tail ↔ circle — same typeCircle ↔ point — different typesAnnulus ↔ disk — different typesCircle ↔ circle — wrong maps"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Same homotopy type: g∘f ≃ idX and f∘g ≃ idY."
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "id": "equivalence-side",
   "text": "On X · ✓ g∘f ≃ id_XOn Y · ✓ f∘g ≃ id_Y"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": null,
   "text": "▶ Play"
  },
  {
   "tag": "output",
   "id": null,
   "text": "0.50"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": "equivalence-connections",
   "text": "Connect points"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "X · filled disk"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Y · one point"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "x · t = 0"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Homotopy Hₜ(x)"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "g(f(x)) · t = 1"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "f(x) · copy"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Going there and back sends the disk to its center. That map is homotopic to the identity."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Same color = same original input. Follow the solid lines around the loop. The dashed lines track the homotopy from the top row to the bottom row."
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Clear circle"
  },
  {
   "tag": "span",
   "id": null,
   "text": "The circled point keeps the color of its original input."
  },
  {
   "tag": "summary",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Why? / The two maps"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "f sends the whole disk to the single point. g sends that point to the disk’s center."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "On X, the composition is the constant map 0. H(x,t) = (1−t)x deforms the identity to this constant map. On the one-point space Y, the other composition is already the identity."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "The top and bottom Y pictures show exactly the same intermediate output. The homotopy is in X: at t = 0 it matches the original input above, and at t = 1 it matches the composition below. The homotopy need not be one-to-one."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Background: Hatcher, homotopy equivalence."
  },
  {
   "tag": "a",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Background: Hatcher, homotopy equivalence."
  }
